            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `backend/backup/manager.py` do?", "a": "Database backup manager for BRIEFR (SQLite and PostgreSQL). SQLite: - Online backup via sqlite3.Connection.backup() (WAL-safe) - PRAGMA integrity_check before and after each backup - Automatic restore on startup when the live DB fails integrity check PostgreSQL (when DATABASE_URL is set): - pg_dump custom-format archive (briefr.pgdump inside the tarball) - pg_restore on manual restore (--clean --if-exists) Both backends: - Tar archives with optio"},
