            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/components/Forge.jsx` do?", "a": "* Forge shell: top view tabs + workspace. Hunt pack docks under the ATT&CK * navigator only (coverage). Technique click toggles selection. Selection * clears when leaving coverage so the panel does not follow other views."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/WallboardPage.jsx` do?", "a": "Product module <code>frontend/src/pages/WallboardPage.jsx</code> (<code>WallboardPage</code>)."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/admin/SecurityPosturePage.jsx` do?", "a": "Operator posture sections (PM-4a); stand-alone ARCH route retired in PM-4c."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/ContextRail.jsx` do?", "a": "* Context rail content for a selected architecture-graph node (spec §5.2 * node selection panel, §8 TM-4: \"node selection populates the context * rail\"). Lives in the persistent right rail (SecurityArchitecturePage.jsx) * so selecting a node never reflows the graph/workspace panel -- the rail * is a fixed-width sticky column (playbook §3 smoothness budget: \"zero * layout shift when selecting a node\")."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/GlobalSearch.jsx` do?", "a": "* Global search (spec §5.17, §8 TM-5): in-module search bar over the corpus * + live MITRE technique names + control titles + API paths (backend * merge.search_corpus / search_mitre_techniques). Arrow-key navigable, * Enter opens the section a result belongs to (§5.17: \"Results grouped by * entity type; arrow-key navigable; Enter opens section + selection\")."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/SecurityArchitecturePage.jsx` do?", "a": "* Security Architecture shell (TM-2, threat-modeling-security-architecture.md * §3.1 + §8): three-panel layout mirroring Forge (FR-2) and Admin -- * left nav / center workspace / persistent context rail, all selection * state round-tripping through the URL (?section=&status=&severity=&type=) * so refresh and deep links never lose context (same fix class as FR-2 P1). * * The nav is manifest-driven (spec §2.2, §8): it renders whatever * `GET /api/s"},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/constants.js` do?", "a": "* TM-2: Security Architecture nav is manifest-driven (spec §2.2, §8 TM-2) -- * there is no hardcoded list of sections here. `humanizeSectionId` turns a * corpus section id (e.g. `trust_boundaries`) into a nav label; the actual * set of sections rendered comes from `GET /api/security-architecture/manifest` * at runtime, so a future TM-3+ section (e.g. `mitre_attack`) appears in the * nav the moment the manifest lists it -- no frontend redeploy nee"},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/AbuseCasesSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Abuse Case Catalog (spec §5.11, §8 TM-5)."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/ArchitectureGraphSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* System Architecture graph (spec §5.2, §8 TM-4): interactive pan/zoom * render of the generated `graphs/architecture.json`. * * No content-sized SVG viewBox — pan/zoom transform works in CSS pixels so * fit-to-view math stays 1:1 with the canvas (avoids double-scale / wrong zoom)."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/AttackSurfaceSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Attack Surface (spec §8 TM-4): generated endpoint inventory × linked controls."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/DecisionsSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Security Decision Records (spec §5.13, §8 TM-5)."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/FrameworkSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* TM-6: shared analyst framework workspace (CWE / OWASP / CAPEC / STRIDE). * * Every framework is one lens on the same live aggregation -- the CWE weakness * classes present in `cves.cwe_ids` across the selected Scope (All CVEs / My * Stack / Watchlist / KEV). The Scope selector is the whole point of the * reframe: the frameworks describe the *user's own* threat surface, not * BRIEFR's. Each row's count drills through to the exact `example_cves` "},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/GenericSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* TM-2 stub section view (spec §8 TM-2: \"even if that view is just a stub * in TM-2, TM-3 builds it out\"). Shows the exact corpus rows behind an * Overview tile click via the generic GET /section/{id} endpoint -- real * data, not mocked, via the shared ArchDataGrid primitive (E5-2)."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/MitreSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* MITRE ATT&CK section (TM-3, spec §5.6). Live coverage matrix grouped by tactic."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/OverviewSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Overview (spec §5.1, §8 TM-2): evidence tiles that are counts or ratios * whose inputs are visible server-side (backend/security_architecture/ * routers/security_architecture.py::get_overview) -- no composite grades, * no arithmetic invented here. Every tile drills through to the exact * corpus rows behind its number via `onDrill(section, filter)`. * * The \"architecture stack\" is a simplified view of the generated layer * (routers / scheduler j"},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/ReviewHistorySection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Review History (spec §5.14, §8 TM-5)."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/RiskRegisterSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Risk Register (spec §5.12, §8 TM-5): ArchDataGrid wrapper over curated + * live risk rows. Two row origins render distinctly (curated vs live, spec * §5.12) and every curated row carries a visible STALE badge sourced from * the server's `stale` flag (security_architecture/merge.py::annotate_stale) * -- never recomputed here, so the badge and the Overview \"Controls Active\" * percentage math always agree on which rows are stale."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/StaleRecordsSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Stale Records (spec §5.1 \"Stale Records\" tile drill-through, §9.6)."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/ThreatScenariosSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Threat Scenarios section (TM-3, spec §5.10)."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/sections/TrustBoundariesSection.jsx` do?", "a": "* Trust Boundaries (spec §5.3, §8 TM-4): vertical flow cards for each * curated boundary crossing. Reads the same GET /section/trust_boundaries * endpoint GenericSection used pre-TM-4 (data shape is a plain curated * record list -- no dedicated backend endpoint needed, spec §4.4's * /trust-boundaries route folds into the existing generic section read), * rendered here as the spec's \"visual vertical flows\" instead of a table."},
            {"category": "overview", "q": "What does `frontend/src/pages/security-architecture/shared/ArchDataGrid.jsx` do?", "a": "ARCH workspace DataGrid — shared primitive with section-scoped styling."},
